  <h1>DSpark: Semi-Autoregressive Decoding with Load-Aware Confidence Scheduling</h1>
  <p class="lead">Parallel draft models are fast but incoherent — they predict every token independently, so "of course" and "no problem" collide into nonsense like "of problem." DSpark inserts a Markov head after a parallel backbone to fix suffix decay, then adds a load-aware confidence scheduler to stop wasting compute verifying tokens that are almost certain to be rejected. The result: +30% accepted length over Eagle3, +16% over DFlash, and +51% production throughput on DeepSeek-V4.</p>
