<!-- Listen-friendly hidden summary -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: DSpark — Semi-Autoregressive Speculative Decoding</h2>
    <p>DSpark from DeepSeek is a new speculative decoding framework that solves two problems with parallel draft models. First, parallel drafters predict every token independently, leading to multi-modal collisions where incoherent combinations like "of problem" get generated because positions don't condition on each other. DSpark adds a lightweight Markov head — a low-rank transition matrix — after the parallel backbone, letting each draft token condition on the previously sampled token. This sequential loop adds negligible latency while lifting accepted length by 16 to 30 percent over DFlash.</p>
    <p>Second, DSpark adds a confidence head that estimates per-position acceptance probability, paired with a hardware-aware scheduler that dynamically prunes low-confidence draft token tails based on current system load. At moderate load it verifies everything; under high concurrency it truncates aggressively, routing compute only to tokens with a positive expected return. In offline benchmarks on Qwen3-4B, DSpark improves accepted length by 30.9 percent over Eagle3 and 16.3 percent over DFlash. In production on DeepSeek-V4, DSpark delivers 51 to 52 percent higher aggregate throughput and 60 to 85 percent faster per-user generation at matched capacity.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：DSpark — 半自回归投机解码</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek 的 DSpark 是一套新的投机解码框架，解决了并行草稿模型的两个核心问题。首先，并行草稿器独立预测每个词元，会产生多模态碰撞——由于各位置之间缺乏依赖，可能生成"of problem"这样不连贯的组合。DSpark 在并行主干网络之后加入了一个轻量级 Markov 头——一个低秩转移矩阵——让每个草稿词元能够基于上一个已采样词元进行条件化。这个顺序循环几乎不增加延迟，却能将接受长度提升 16 到 30 个百分点。</p>
    <p>其次，DSpark 增加了一个置信度头，用于估计每个位置的接受概率，并配合感知硬件负载的调度器，根据当前系统负载动态裁剪低置信度的草稿词元尾部。在较低负载时验证全部词元；高并发时则积极截断，仅将计算资源用于期望收益为正的词元。在 Qwen3-4B 的离线基准测试中，DSpark 的接受长度比 Eagle3 提升 30.9%，比 DFlash 提升 16.3%。在 DeepSeek-V4 的生产环境中，DSpark 在相同容量下实现了 51 到 52% 的吞吐量提升和 60 到 85% 的每用户生成速度提升。</p>
